    # bc_admits_blocked as BUCKET-4 because upstream's whole test IS
    # `outlives_indir::<'_, 'b, _>(&mut 1u32)`. ⚠ A ROW IS ALREADY WAITING BEHIND IT:
    # two probes written this round that pin `'b` INVARIANTLY instead of with a turbofish
    # (`w: &mut &'b i64`, and `struct Inv<'b> { f: fn(&'b i64) -> &'b i64 }`, each against
    # `fn outlives_indir<'a,'b>(x: &'a mut i64, w: ..) where 'a: 'b` called with
    # `&mut 1i64`) are BOTH ADMITTED where rustc refuses. To make it a row: decide whether
    # the invariant form is a re-port (it is not — it substitutes the construct) or its own
    # finding, and if the latter, write it as a native fixture with its own root.
